hadiths[111]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16953","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, he said: My father, and Abu Amir al-Aqadi, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Isa ibn Talha, Abu Amir said in his hadith, he said: Isa ibn Talha narrated to me, he said: We entered upon Muawiya, then the caller called to prayer. So he said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great. So Muawiya said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Muawiya said: And I bear witness. Abu Amir said: That there is no god but Allah. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Muawiya said: And I bear witness. Abu Amir said: That Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Yahya said: Then a man narrated to us that when he said: Come to prayer, he said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah. Muawiya said: Thus I heard your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying."
"16954","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Muawiya came to Madina, then he addressed us and brought out a tuft of hair. Then he said: I did not think anyone does it except the Jews. It reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he called it falsehood, or alziyr, Muhammad ibn Jafar doubted."
"16955","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, he said: I heard Abu Mijlaz saying: Muawiya entered upon Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn Amir. He said: So Ibn Amir stood and Ibn al-Zubayr did not stand. He said: And the shaykh was the weightier of the two. He said: He said: Meh. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves that the servants of Allah stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"16956","Abdullah said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr, he is al-Bursani, narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to me that Isa ibn Umar informed him, from Abdullah ibn Alqama ibn Waqqas, from Alqama ibn Waqqas, he said: I was with Muawiya when his caller called the adhan. Then Muawiya said as the caller said, until when he said: Come to prayer, he said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah. Then when he said: Come to success, he said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah. And he said after that what the caller said. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that."
"16957","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that Muawiya entered upon Aisha. So she said to him: Did you not fear that I would set a man for you and kill you? Then he said: You would not do it while I am in a house of safety, and I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, meaning: Faith restrains killing. How am I in what is between me and you and in your needs? She said: Righteous. He said: Then leave us and them until we meet our Lord, Mighty and Majestic."
"16958","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, he said: I was among a company of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Muawiya. Then Muawiya said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing silk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, Exalted is He, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing gold except cut pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, Exalted is He, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade riding leopard skins? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, Exalted is He, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinking in silver vessels? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, Exalted is He, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade combining Hajj and Umra? They said: As for this, no. He said: Yet it is with them."
"16959","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, he said: Jabala ibn Atiya informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah intends good for a slave, He gives him understanding in religion."
"16960","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, he said: Abu Naama al-Sadi narrated to me, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Muawiya went out to a circle in the mosque. Then he said: What seated you? They said: We sat remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: By Allah, nothing seated you except that? They said: By Allah, nothing seated us except that. He said: As for me, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you, and there was none of my station from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with fewer hadiths from him than me. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to a circle of his companions. Then he said: What seated you? They said: We sat remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and praising Him for guiding us to Islam and favoring us with you. He said: By Allah, nothing seated you except that? They said: By Allah, nothing seated us except that. He said: As for me, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and informed me that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasts of you to the angels."
"16961","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, Qays informed us, from Ata, that Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Harb took from the ends, meaning the hair of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the days of the ten, with a barbed arrowhead with me, while he was in ihram, and the people disapproved of that."
"16962","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, from Mabad al-Juhani, he said: Muawiya seldom narrated anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would say these words, seldom omitting them or narrating them on Fridays from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. And this wealth is sweet and green. So whoever takes it by its right, it is blessed for him therein. And beware of excessive praise, for it is slaughter."
"16963","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed me, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not precede me in bowing nor in prostration, for whatever I precede you in when I bow, you will catch me when I rise, and whatever I precede you in when I prostrate, you will catch me when I rise. I have become bulky."
"16964","Waki narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, he said: Muawiya said upon the minbar: O Allah, there is no preventer of what You give, nor giver of what You prevent, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail against You. Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon this minbar."
"16965","Waki narrated to us, Abu al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Muawiya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not ride khazz nor nimar. Ibn Sirin said: And Muawiya was not accused concerning hadith from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is called al-Habari, meaning Abu al-Mutamir, and Yazid ibn Tahman is this Abu al-Mutamir."
"16966","Waki narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Muawiya, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to repeat with the callers."
"16967","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bahz said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Jabala ibn Atiya, from Ibn Muhayriz, Bahz said: Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a slave, He gives him understanding in religion."
"16968","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Abd al-Samad said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Said, he said: Muawiya said one day: You have innovated an evil adornment. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade false hair. And Abd al-Samad said: False hair. He said: And a man came with a staff upon its head a rag. Then he said: Verily this is false hair. Abu Amir said: Qatada said: It is what women use to thicken their hair with rags."
"16969","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Maymun al-Qannad, from Abu Qilaba, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade riding nimar and wearing gold except cut pieces."
"16970","Ismail narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, that Muawiya entered a house wherein were Ibn Amir and Ibn al-Zubayr. Then Ibn Amir stood and Ibn al-Zubayr sat. So Muawiya said to him: Sit, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever is pleased that servants stand for him, let him take a house in the Fire."
"16971","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj, he said: Shuba informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Mabad al-Juhani, he said: Muawiya seldom narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he would seldom fail on Friday to narrate these words from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. And this wealth is sweet and green. So whoever takes it by its right, it is blessed for him therein. And beware of excessive praise, for it is slaughter."
"16972","Arim narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from al-Mughira, from Mabad al-Qass, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd, from Muawiya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever drinks wine, flog him. Then if he returns, flog him. Then if he returns, flog him. Then if he returns a fourth time, kill him."
"16973","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Hariz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf al-Jurashi, from Muawiya, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sucking his tongue, or he said: His lip, meaning al-Hasan ibn Ali, blessings of Allah be upon him. And a tongue or two lips which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sucked shall never be punished."
"16974","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Jafar narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: I heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan mention a hadith he narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I never heard him narrate from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, any hadith besides it, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. And a band of Muslims shall continue fighting upon the truth, dominant over those who oppose them, until the Day of Resurrection."
"16975","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, from Muawiya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon these boards: O Allah, there is no preventer of what You give, nor giver of what You prevent, nor does the fortune of the fortunate avail against You. Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"16976","Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murra informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab saying: Muawiya addressed upon the minbar of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or the minbar of Madina, and brought out a tuft of hair. He said: I did not think anyone does this other than the Jews. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called it falsehood."
"16977","Bishr ibn Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, he said: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim used to narrate that it reached Muawiya, while he was with him in a delegation of Quraysh, that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrates that there will be a king from Qahtan. So Muawiya became angry, then stood and praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as He deserves. Then he said: To proceed, it has reached me that men among you narrate hadiths that are not in the Book of Allah nor transmitted from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Those are your ignorant ones. So beware of fancies that mislead their people, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: This rule is in Quraysh; none contends with them for it except Allah casts him upon his face, as long as they uphold the religion."
"16978","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us, he said: Abu Abd Rabbihi narrated to me, he said: I heard Muawiya saying upon this minbar: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: What remains of the world is trial and tribulation. And the likeness of the deed of one of you is as the likeness of a vessel: when its top is good, its bottom is good, and when its top is corrupt, its bottom is corrupt."
"16979","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu al-Azhar, from Muawiya, that he described to them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and that he wiped his head with a handful of water until water dripped from his head, or almost dripped, and that he showed them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then when he reached wiping the head, he placed his palms upon the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the nape, then returned them until he reached the place he began from."
"16980","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Walid, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ala narrated to us, that he heard Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Malik, and Abu al-Azhar narrating from the ablution of Muawiya, he said: He shows them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he performed ablution three times three times, and washed his feet without number."
"16981","Yaqub and Sad said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj narrated to me that al-Abbas ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas married Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam to his daughter, and Abd al-Rahman married him to his daughter, and they had made a dowry. Then Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, while caliph, wrote to Marwan ordering him to separate them, and said in his letter: This is the shighar which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade."
"16982","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from his father Abbad, he said: When Muawiya came to us performing Hajj, we came with him to Makkah. He said: So he prayed with us Zuhr two rakas, then departed to Dar al-Nadwa. He said: And Uthman, when he completed the prayer upon coming to Makkah, would pray therein Zuhr and Asr and the last Isha four by four. Then when he went out to Mina and Arafat, he shortened the prayer. Then when he finished Hajj and stayed at Mina, he completed the prayer until he left Makkah. Then when he prayed with us Zuhr two rakas, Marwan ibn al-Hakam and Amr ibn Uthman rose to him and said to him: None has faulted your cousin with anything uglier than what you faulted him with. Then he said to them: And what is that? He said: Then they said to him: Do you not know that he completed the prayer at Makkah. He said: Then he said to them: Woe to you, was there anything other than what I did? I prayed them with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah Exalted be pleased with them. They said: Your cousin had completed it, and your differing from him is a fault against him. He said: Then Muawiya went out to Asr and prayed it with us four."
"16983","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj, he said: Shuba narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatada narrating from Abu al-Tufayl, Hajjaj said in his hadith, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl saying: Muawiya and Ibn Abbas came, then Ibn Abbas circumambulated and touched all the corners. Then Muawiya said to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only touched the two Yamani corners. Ibn Abbas said: None of its corners is abandoned. Hajjaj said: Shuba said: People differ in this hadith, saying Muawiya is the one who said: None of the House is abandoned, but he preserved it from Qatada thus."
"16984","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, that he heard Asim ibn Bahdala narrating from Abu Salih, from Muawiya, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When they drink wine, flog them, then when they drink, flog them, then when they drink, flog them, then when they drink it a fourth time, kill them."
"16985","Ibn Numayr and Yala said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, and Abu Badr, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Muawiya, Yala said in his hadith: I heard Muawiya saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying upon these boards: O Allah, there is no preventer of what You give, nor giver of what You prevent. Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion."
"16986","Ibn Numayr and Yala said: Talha, meaning Ibn Yahya, narrated to us, from Isa ibn Talha, he said: I heard Muawiya saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The callers have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection."
"16987","Yala and Yazid ibn Harun said: Mujammi ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I was beside Abu Umama ibn Sahl while he was facing the caller, and the caller said Allahu Akbar twice, so Abu Umama said Allahu Akbar twice, and he bore witness that there is no god but Allah twice, so Abu Umama bore witness twice, and the caller bore witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah twice, and Abu Umama bore witness twice. Then he turned to me and said: Thus Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16988","Abu Amr Marwan ibn Shuja al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to us, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that Muawiya informed him that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shorten his hair with a barbed arrowhead. So we said to Ibn Abbas: This reached us only from Muawiya. Then he said: Muawiya was not suspect against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"16989","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Shaykh al-Hunai, that Muawiya said to a group of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade leopard skins to be ridden upon? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And do you know that he forbade wearing gold except cut pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And do you know that he forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: And do you know that he forbade muta, meaning the muta of Hajj? They said: O Allah, no."
"16990","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he saw Muawiya addressing upon the minbar, with in his hand a lock of hair. He said: I heard him saying: Where are your scholars, O people of Madina? I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding the like of this, and he said: The Children of Israel were only punished when their women adopted these."
"16991","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me that Nafi ibn Jubayr sent him to al-Saib ibn Yazid, son of the sister of Namir, asking him about something Muawiya saw from him in prayer. So he said: Yes, I prayed with him Friday in the enclosure. Then when he gave salam, I stood in my place and prayed. Then when he entered, he sent to me and said: Do not repeat what you did. When you pray Friday, do not join it with a prayer until you speak or go out, for the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that: It is not joined with a prayer until one goes out or speaks."
"16992","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me that he heard Muawiya addressing at Madina, saying: O people of Madina, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: This is the day of Ashura, and fasting it was not prescribed for us. So whoever of you wishes to fast, let him fast, for I am fasting. So the people fasted."
"16993","Rawh narrated to us, Malik and Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan on the day of Ashura in the year he performed Hajj, while upon the minbar, and he mentioned the hadith."
"16994","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Dhakwan, from Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said concerning the drinker of wine: When he drinks wine, flog him, then when he drinks, flog him, then when he drinks a third time, flog him, then when he drinks a fourth time, strike his neck."
"16995","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, that Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, Rawh said: Informed him, he said: I shortened from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a barbed arrowhead at Marwa, or I saw him shortened from with a barbed arrowhead at Marwa."
"16996","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us that Sad ibn Ibrahim informed him, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, that Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari informed him that he was sitting among a group of the Ansar, then Muawiya went out to them and asked them about their talk. Then they said: We were in a talk of the Ansar. Then Muawiya said: Shall I not add to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? They said: Yes, O Commander of the Believers. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates him."
"16997","Rawh narrated to us, Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ali, a man of Banu Abd Shams, narrated to me, my father said, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith, and Umar ibn Said narrated to me that Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Ali informed him, from his father, he said: I heard Muawiya upon the minbar at Makkah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wearing gold and silk."
"16998","Rawh narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir ibn Sad saying: I heard Jarir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan saying, while he was addressing: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died while he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr, may Allah Exalted be pleased with him, died while he was sixty-three years old, and Umar died while he was sixty-three years old. Muawiya said: And I today am sixty-three years old."
"16999","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Jabala ibn Atiya, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Muawiya, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a slave, He gives him understanding in religion. Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this speech at the end of this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting, joined to it, and it had been crossed out, so I do not know whether he read it to me or not: And the hearing, obedient one has no proof against him, and the hearing, disobedient one has no proof for him."
"17000","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Muawiya, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever dies without an imam dies a death of Jahiliya."
"17001","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb - meaning Ibn Shaddad - narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i narrated to me, from his brother Himman, that Mu'awiyah, in the year he performed Hajj, gathered a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Ka'bah and said: I ask you about some things, so inform me. I adjure you by Allah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wearing silk? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wearing gold? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wearing tiger fur? They said: Yes. He said: And I bear witness."
"17002","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Jarad, a man of Banu Tamim, from Raja' ibn Haywah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."
"17003","Struck through. Abdullah narrated to us, he said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting: Bakr ibn Yazid narrated to us - and I think I heard it from him during study but I did not write it down - and Bakr used to live in al-Madinah; I think he was there during the Mihnah; this hadith had been struck through in his book. He said: Bakr ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr - meaning Ibn Abi Maryam - informed us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays al-Kilabi, that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two eyes are the fastening of the anus, so when the two eyes sleep, the fastening comes loose."
"17004","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi, he informed him, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends good for a servant, He gives him understanding in the religion."
"17005","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Amir ibn Abdullah al-Yahsabi. Abdullah said: My father said thus - Yahya ibn Ishaq said - and it is in fact Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi - he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain a group of my ummah upon the truth, not caring who opposes them or forsakes them, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes."
"17006","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu al-Safar, from Amir, from Jarir, he said: I was with Mu'awiyah and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, died when he was sixty-three years old, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, died when he was sixty-three years old."
"17007","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Umra is permissible for its people."
"17008","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Naqid narrated to me, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Mu'awiyah said to me: Did you know that I trimmed from the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a mishqas? So I said to him: I do not know this except as a proof against you."
"17009","Abdullah narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Mu'awiyah, he said: I trimmed from the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah."
"17010","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ja'far, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Mu'awiyah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimming with a mishqas."
"17011","Abdullah narrated to us, Ismail Abu Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, they said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, he said: Mu'awiyah said to Ibn Abbas: Did you not know that I trimmed from the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a mishqas? So Ibn Abbas said: No. Ibn Abbad said in his hadith: Ibn Abbas said: And this is a proof against Mu'awiyah."
"17012","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, kill him."
"17013","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when he finished the prayer: O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail him against You."
"17014","Amr ibn al-Haytham Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Jarir, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr died when he was sixty-three, and Umar died when he was sixty-three, and I am today sixty-three years old."
"17015","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah: he heard Mu'awiyah say, in al-Madinah upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Where are your scholars, O people of al-Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on this day, the day of Ashura, saying: Whoever among you wishes to fast it, let him fast it. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the like of this - and he brought out a tuft of hair from his sleeve - and he said: The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted these."
"17016","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not race me in bowing and prostration, for I have grown heavy in body, and whatever I precede you with when I bow, you will catch up with me when I rise, and whatever I precede you with when I prostrate, you will catch up with me when I rise."
"17017","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ibn Munabbih, from his brother, from Mu'awiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not press insistently in asking. By Allah, no one asks me for anything and his request comes forth for him but that blessing is placed in it for him."
"17018","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Muhammad ibn Ka'b - meaning al-Qurazi - narrated to me, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah preaching upon this minbar, saying: Know that there is none to withhold what He gives, and none to give what He withholds, Allah, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against Him. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon these sticks."
"17019","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Tawus, that Ibn Abbas informed him that Mu'awiyah informed him, he said: I trimmed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a mishqas, or he said: I saw him being trimmed with a mishqas at al-Marwah."
"17020","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: We were with Mu'awiyah, and the mu'adhdhin said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, so Mu'awiyah said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, so Mu'awiyah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Then he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then he said: Come to prayer, so he said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. Then he said: Come to success, so he said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. Then he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, so he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. Then he said: There is no god but Allah, he said: There is no god but Allah. Then he said: Thus would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say - or: your Prophet - when the mu'adhdhin called."
"17021","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Ibn Abbas and Mu'awiyah performed Hajj, and Ibn Abbas began touching all the corners, so Mu'awiyah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only touched these two Yemeni corners. So Ibn Abbas said: None of its corners is to be abandoned."
"17022","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Isa ibn Talhah, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah say, when the mu'adhdhin came to him announcing the prayer: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The mu'adhdhins will be the longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection."
"17023","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Talhah - meaning Ibn Yahya - narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Mu'awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nothing befalls the believer in his body that hurts him except that Allah expiates thereby some of his evil deeds."
"17024","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed those who split speech as poetry is split."
"17025","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Bayhas ibn Fahdan narrated to me, from Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i, I heard it from him, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except cut in pieces."
"17026","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Mujammi' ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Mu'awiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to repeat with the mu'adhdhins."
"17027","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Ma'bad al-Juhani, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah - and he narrated little from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he would hardly ever preach except that he mentioned this hadith in his sermon: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This wealth is sweet and green, so whoever takes it rightfully, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will bless it for him. And whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion. And beware of praise, for it is slaughter."
"17028","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said therein: And beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter."
"17029","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible for its people."
"17030","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hariz ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf al-Jurashi narrated to us, from Abu Hind al-Bajali, he said: We were with Mu'awiyah while he was upon his bed, having closed his eyes, and we discussed hijrah, some of us saying it has ended and some of us saying it has not ended. So Mu'awiyah woke up and said: What were you discussing? So we informed him - and he would rarely narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he said: We discussed at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Hijrah does not end until repentance ends, and repentance does not end until the sun rises from its west."
"17031","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid informed us, from Abu Awn, from Abu Idris, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah - and he narrated little from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except a man who dies a disbeliever, or a man who kills a believer deliberately."
"17032","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating from Mu'awiyah, he said: You pray a prayer - we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we did not see him pray it, and he forbade them - meaning the two rak'ahs after Asr."
"17033","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i, that he witnessed Mu'awiyah while with him was a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Mu'awiyah said to them: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding on tiger skins? They said: Yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in silver vessels? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold except cut in pieces? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining between Hajj and Umrah? They said: O Allah, no. He said: By Allah, it is indeed with them."
"17034","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah narrating while saying: Beware of the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a hadith that was current in the time of Umar, and Umar, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, was the most fearful of people regarding Allah, Mighty and Majestic. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion."
"17035","And I heard him say: I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who gives. So whomever I give a gift from a willing soul, it is that it be blessed for one of you, and whomever I give a gift from greed and greedy asking, he is like one who eats and is not satisfied."
"17036","And I heard him say: There will always remain a nation of my ummah manifest upon the truth; whoever opposes them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are manifest over the people."
"17037","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ata' ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me that Nafi' ibn Jubayr sent him to al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, son of the sister of Namir, asking him about something Mu'awiyah had seen in him in prayer. He said: Yes, I prayed with him Friday in the Maqsurah, and when he gave salam, I stood in my place and prayed. When he entered, he sent for me and said: Do not repeat what you did. When you pray Friday, do not join it to another prayer until you go out or speak, for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that: that one prayer not be joined to another prayer until one goes out or speaks."
"17038","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating from Mu'awiyah that he saw people praying after Asr, and he said: You pray a prayer - we accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we did not see him pray it, and he forbade it - meaning the two rak'ahs after Asr."
"17039","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Amr ibn Uthman, informed me, from his father, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever forgets something in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"17040","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17041","Yunus narrated to us, Layth - meaning Ibn Sa'd - narrated to us, from Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ajlan - from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, freedman of Uthman, from his father Yusuf, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that he prayed before them and stood in the prayer while sitting was due upon him, so the people glorified Allah, but he completed his standing. Then we prostrated two prostrations while sitting after he completed the prayer. Then he sat upon the minbar and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever forgets something in his prayer, let him prostrate the like of these two prostrations."
"17042","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: Mu'awiyah came out and they stood for him, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves that men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"17043","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us that Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed him, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, that Yazid ibn Jariyah informed him that he was sitting among a group of the Ansar, and Mu'awiyah came out to them and asked them about their conversation. They said: We were in a conversation from the talk of the Ansar. So Mu'awiyah said: Shall I not add to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes, O Commander of the Believers. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates him."
"17044","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, he said: al-Hakam ibn Mina informed me, from Yazid ibn Jariyah, he said: I was indeed in the assembly of Mu'awiyah among a group of the Ansar, and we were talking, when Mu'awiyah came out to us, and he mentioned its meaning."
"17045","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Yahsabi, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, who gives. So whomever I give a gift with a willing soul, it will be blessed for him in it, and whomever I give a gift with greed of soul and greed of asking, he is like one who eats and is not satisfied."
"17046","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when the mu'adhdhin called - say the like of what he says."
"17047","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Ali informed me, my father informed me that he heard Mu'awiyah preaching in the shade of the Ka'bah while saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold ornament and wearing silk."
"17048","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the mu'adhdhin say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, would say the like of his saying, and when he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he would say the like of his saying, and when he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he would say the like of his saying."
"17049","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali, from Jarir, that he heard Mu'awiyah preaching, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died when he was sixty-three, and Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, when he was sixty-three, and Umar when he was sixty-three, and I am sixty-three."
"17050","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When he drinks wine, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, kill him."
"17051","He said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Mubashshir, freedman of Umm Habibah, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Attab, from Mu'awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who adds to her hair from the hair of another, she only adds it falsely."
"17052","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their best in Jahiliyyah are their best in Islam, when they understand. By Allah, were it not that Quraysh become arrogant, I would inform them what the best of them have with Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"17053","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail him against You. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion. And the best women who rode camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: most caring toward a husband in his means, and most tender toward a child in his childhood."
"17054","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me that Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Ali al-Adawi informed him that his father informed him, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah upon the minbar in Makkah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold and silk."
"17055","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Layth - meaning Ibn Sa'd - informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Bakr, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion. And this ummah will always remain an ummah established upon the command of Allah; whoever opposes them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are manifest over the people."
"17056","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, that Umayr ibn Hani' narrated to him, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan upon this minbar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will always remain a group of my ummah established upon the command of Allah; whoever forsakes them or opposes them will not harm them, until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes while they are manifest over the people. So Malik ibn Yukhamir al-Saksaki stood and said: O Commander of the Believers, I heard Mu'adh ibn Jabal say: And they are the people of al-Sham. So Mu'awiyah said, raising his voice: This is Malik claiming that he heard Mu'adh say: And they are the people of al-Sham."
"17057","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather narrating that Mu'awiyah took the water-skin after Abu Hurayrah, following the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with it, while Abu Hurayrah complained. While he was performing wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he raised his head to him once or twice and said: O Mu'awiyah, if you are put in charge of a matter, fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and be just. He said: I kept thinking I would be afflicted with office because of the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until I was afflicted."
"17058","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan came to al-Madinah, and it was the last coming he came, and he brought out a ball of hair and said: I did not think anyone does this except the Jews, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called it falsehood. He said: As if he meant joining hair."
"17059","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ayyash - meaning Ismail - narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar and others, from Abu Hariz, freedman of Mu'awiyah, he said: Mu'awiyah addressed the people in Hims and mentioned in his sermon that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seven things, and I convey them to you and forbid you them. Among them: wailing, poetry, images, display of adornment, skins of beasts of prey, gold, and silk."
"17060","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a conveyor, and Allah guides; and a distributor, and Allah gives. So whoever receives from me something with good desire and good guidance, that is what will be blessed for him in it. And whoever receives from me something with evil desire and evil guidance, that is one who eats and is not satisfied."
"17061","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Abdullah al-Hawzani narrated to me - Abu al-Mughirah said in another place: al-Harazi - from Abu Amir Abdullah ibn Luhayy, he said: We performed Hajj with Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and when we arrived in Makkah, he stood after praying Zuhr and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the two Books split in their religion into seventy-two sects, and this ummah will split into seventy-three sects - meaning desires - all of them in the Fire except one, and it is the Jama'ah. And there will emerge among my ummah peoples through whom those desires course as rabies courses through its victim, leaving no vein nor joint but it enters it. By Allah, O assembly of Arabs, if you do not uphold what your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought, others among people are more likely not to uphold it."
"17062","Marwan ibn Shuja' narrated to us, he said: Khusayf narrated to me, from Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that Mu'awiyah informed him that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimming his hair with a mishqas. So I said to Ibn Abbas: This matter has not reached us except from Mu'awiyah. So he said: Mu'awiyah was not accused against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17063","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Bashshar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Mu'ammal and Abu Ahmad - or one of them - narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Mu'awiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimmed with a mishqas."
